---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---
<PageLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="What Sublime Pantry collects (very little), what stays in your browser, and how newsletter emails are used." path="/privacy" breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Privacy", href: "/privacy" }]}>
  <span class="kicker">Policy</span>
  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  <p><em>Effective August 31, 2026.</em></p>
  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Newsletter signups:</strong> your email address, used only to send The Dry Batch newsletter. Unsubscribe links are in every issue. We never sell or share subscriber lists.</li>
    <li><strong>Contact form:</strong> the name, email, and message you send us, used only to reply.</li>
    <li><strong>Hosting logs:</strong> our host (Netlify) processes standard server logs (IP address, user agent) to serve the site.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
  <p>The <a href="/tools/batch-log">Batch Log tool</a> stores your batch records in your own browser's local storage. That data never leaves your device and we cannot see it. Clearing your browser data deletes it, so use the CSV export for backups.</p>
  <h2>Tracking</h2>
  <p>We do not run third-party advertising trackers. If we add analytics, we will use a privacy-respecting provider and update this policy first.</p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Privacy questions: use the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.</p>
</PageLayout>
